# lines marked STALE need updating — after fixing the text, delete the [hash] and re-run the tool.


@event y3_career_fair
# en: The Career Fair
title [a6ba30] = 职业招聘会
# en: Every guild, order and institution in the kingdom has sent someone to the great hall. They are all very polite. They are all, very clearly, shopping. Where will you leave your name?
text [5b87fc] = 王国里每个公会、教团和机构都派了人到大礼堂来。他们都非常客气。他们也都非常明显地在挑人。你要把名字留在哪里？
# en: The great hall lined with recruiters' booths — a Conclave mage in silver, a librarian behind a wall of books, a circus ringmaster juggling fire.
scene [7e3280] = 大礼堂里摆满了招聘摊位——一位身着银袍的议会法师、一位坐在书墙后的图书管理员、一位抛着火把的马戏团团长。
# en: The Conclave of the Seven Towers
opt.conclave.label [c832a4] = 七塔议会
# en: Apprentice archmages. The interview tests your Arcana.
opt.conclave.hint [04186b] = 大法师学徒。面试考你的奥术。
# en: The Royal Library
opt.library.label [64f580] = 皇家图书馆
# en: Keepers of every book ever written. The interview tests your Lore.
opt.library.hint [e1ce52] = 世上每一本书的守护者。面试考你的学识。
# en: The Guild of Alchemists
opt.guild.label [8a8f99] = 炼金师公会
# en: Potions, profit, explosions. The interview tests your Alchemy.
opt.guild.hint [acaaa6] = 药水、利润、爆炸。面试考你的炼金。
# en: The Crown's Office of Unseen Affairs
opt.unseen.label [a4101a] = 王室隐秘事务署
# en: They found you, actually. The interview tests your Guile.
opt.unseen.hint [606647] = 其实是他们先找到你的。面试考你的诡计。
# en: The Travelling Circus of Wonders
opt.circus.label [f3ec0c] = 奇迹巡回马戏团
# en: Wagons, crowds, illusions. The interview tests your Charm.
opt.circus.hint [6df8a7] = 马车、人群、幻术。面试考你的魅力。
# en: Stay at Lumenhold as a junior teacher
opt.teaching.label [27030b] = 留在流明堡当见习教师
# en: Needs a faculty member who trusts you: Thorne, Maud or the Headmistress.
opt.teaching.hint [e8bcda] = 需要一位信任你的教职员：索恩教授、老莫德或院长。
# en: Nobody on the faculty knows you well enough to vouch for you.
opt.teaching.locked [bbf1f9] = 教职员里没有谁足够了解你，能为你担保。
# en: Not yet — you'd rather not decide
opt.none.label [0a96fd] = 还不急——你暂时不想决定
# en: You collect a tote bag, three pamphlets and a free quill. {month < 4: The future can wait one more month; the fair is back next month.|The fair packs up for good. The future will have to come and find you.}
opt.none.say.1 [0f9734] = 你领了一个帆布袋、三本小册子和一支免费的羽毛笔。{month < 4: 未来可以再等一个月；招聘会下个月还会来。|招聘会彻底收摊了。未来只能自己来找你了。}

@event y3_interview
# en: The Interview
title [7d775f] = 面试
# en: Three people behind a long table. One takes notes; one smiles too much; one says nothing at all, which is clearly the one who decides. "Tell us," says the smiling one, "why you."
text [06648e] = 长桌后坐着三个人。一个做笔记；一个笑得太多；一个一言不发——显然，做决定的就是这一位。“说说看，”爱笑的那位开口，“为什么是你？”
# en: A small panelled room, a long table, three interviewers and one empty chair facing them.
scene [05e47c] = 一间镶着护墙板的小房间，一张长桌，三位面试官，对面一把空椅子。
# en: Let your record speak
opt.left.label [1ea228] = 让履历说话
# en: You talk about what you've learned and, more importantly, what you got wrong and fixed. The silent one writes a single word. You suspect it's "yes".
opt.left.say.1 [c8179c] = 你讲你学到了什么，更重要的是，你搞错过什么、又是怎么改正的。沉默的那位只写下一个词。你猜那是“行”。
# en: You recite your achievements like a shopping list. The silent one looks at the clock. "Now," says the smiling one, "a small practical."
opt.left.say.2 [2da86c] = 你像念购物清单一样背诵自己的成就。沉默的那位看了一眼钟。“现在，”爱笑的那位说，“来个小小的实操。”
# en: Tell them a story
opt.right.label [a082be] = 给他们讲个故事
# en: You tell them about the night the lake froze, or the night you caught a star, or the night you were wrong. The silent one laughs. Out loud.
opt.right.say.1 [1b6366] = 你讲起湖面结冰的那一夜，或者你接住一颗星星的那一夜，或者你犯错的那一夜。沉默的那位笑了。出声地笑了。
# en: The story goes on too long and ends in the wrong place. Somewhere in the middle you lost them, and yourself. "Now," says the smiling one, "a small practical."
opt.right.say.2 [4096b3] = 故事讲得太长，结尾也落错了地方。讲到一半，你就把他们弄丢了，也把自己弄丢了。“现在，”爱笑的那位说，“来个小小的实操。”

@event y3_interview_practical
# en: The Practical
title [eaf727] = 实操
# en: The note-taker sets a task on the table. {flag(career_conclave): A ward with a flaw in it, somewhere.|{flag(career_library): A crumbling manuscript in three hands and no catalogue.|{flag(career_guild): A cauldron, a recipe with one ingredient missing, and a clock.|{flag(career_unseen): A sealed letter, and the request to read it without breaking the seal.|{flag(career_circus): An empty stage, a sceptical crowd of three, and five minutes.|A class of imaginary first-years, and a lesson to give them.}}}}} "In your own time," says the smiling one, and turns over an hourglass.
text [2862ee] = 记录的那位在桌上摆出一项任务。{flag(career_conclave): 一道结界，某处有个破绽。|{flag(career_library): 一份出自三人之手、没有目录、正在碎裂的手稿。|{flag(career_guild): 一口坩埚，一张缺了一味材料的配方，还有一只钟。|{flag(career_unseen): 一封封好的信，要求你不拆封蜡读出内容。|{flag(career_circus): 一个空舞台，三个将信将疑的观众，还有五分钟。|一群想象中的一年级生，和一堂要给他们上的课。}}}}} “不急，”爱笑的那位说着，把一只沙漏翻了过来。
# en: A plain table in a panelled room set with a single task, three interviewers watching a student roll up their sleeves.
scene [9735fb] = 镶板房间里一张朴素的桌子上摆着一项任务，三位面试官看着一个学生卷起袖子。
# en: Do it properly
opt.left.label [859632] = 认真完成
# en: You find the flaw, name it and close it, and the ward rings like a struck glass. The silent one leans forward for the first time.
opt.left.say.1 [19a282] = 你找到了破绽，说出它，然后补上，结界像被敲响的玻璃一样鸣响。沉默的那位第一次身体前倾。
# en: The flaw finds you first. The ward fizzes out in your hands, and the note-taker writes for a long time.
opt.left.say.2 [4a3fa4] = 破绽先找上了你。结界在你手里嘶嘶地熄灭了，记录的那位写了很久。
# en: Three hands, three centuries, one lost chapter. You date them all before the sand runs out. The silent one nods, once.
opt.left.say.3 [7bd96d] = 三种笔迹，三个世纪，一个遗失的章节。沙子漏完之前，你把它们的年代全断了出来。沉默的那位点了一下头。
# en: You date the second hand a century wrong, and know it the moment you say it. The note-taker writes for a long time.
opt.left.say.4 [c75925] = 你把第二种笔迹的年代断错了一个世纪，话一出口就知道了。记录的那位写了很久。
# en: You find the missing ingredient by its absence and the cauldron settles to a perfect simmer. Someone behind the table sniffs, approvingly.
opt.left.say.5 [220baa] = 你凭着缺失察觉出那味少了的材料，坩埚安定下来，完美地文火慢炖。桌子后面有人嗅了嗅，表示赞许。
# en: The cauldron spits and turns a colour no recipe asks for. The note-taker writes for a long time.
opt.left.say.6 [796d95] = 坩埚噼啪作响，变成了一种没有配方会要求的颜色。记录的那位写了很久。
# en: Steam, a thin blade, a little patience. You read it, reseal it and hand it back. The silent one smiles, which is somehow worse.
opt.left.say.7 [a79e9e] = 蒸汽、一片薄刃、一点耐心。你读完，重新封好，递了回去。沉默的那位笑了，不知怎么这更吓人。
# en: The seal cracks with a sound like a shot. The silent one does not look surprised. The note-taker writes for a long time.
opt.left.say.8 [e395b2] = 封蜡裂开，声音像一声枪响。沉默的那位毫不意外。记录的那位写了很久。
# en: Five minutes of nonsense and wonder, and the crowd of three are on their feet. One of them is the silent one.
opt.left.say.9 [c96f52] = 五分钟的胡闹与奇迹，三个观众站了起来。其中一个就是沉默的那位。
# en: The crowd of three stays seated, arms folded, for all five minutes. The note-taker writes for a long time.
opt.left.say.10 [e66680] = 整整五分钟，三个观众抱着胳膊坐着没动。记录的那位写了很久。
# en: You teach the empty chairs the thing you most wish someone had taught you, and forget for a while that they're empty. The silent one nods.
opt.left.say.11 [efb9c1] = 你把自己最希望当年有人教给你的东西教给了那些空椅子，有一阵子忘了它们是空的。沉默的那位点了点头。
# en: You lose the imaginary class in the first minute, which you hadn't known was possible. The note-taker writes for a long time.
opt.left.say.12 [a516ac] = 你在第一分钟就镇不住那群想象中的学生了，你都不知道这还有可能。记录的那位写了很久。
# en: Ask questions before you start
opt.right.label [00676d] = 开始前先提问
# en: You ask three good questions, then do the task carefully and well. It's slower than they'd like. The silent one doesn't seem to mind.
opt.right.say.1 [97b7a6] = 你提了三个好问题，然后仔细、出色地完成了任务。比他们希望的慢一些。沉默的那位似乎并不介意。
# en: You ask three good questions and run out of sand before you've finished. "Careful," says the smiling one, in a tone that isn't quite praise.
opt.right.say.2 [50d652] = 你提了三个好问题，结果沙子漏完了还没做完。“仔细点，”爱笑的那位说，那语气算不上夸奖。

@event y3_interview_question
# en: The Silent One's Question
title [740fdd] = 沉默者的问题
# en: At last the silent one speaks. "Tell me about a time you did something you weren't proud of," they say, "and whether you'd do it again."
text [d81e5e] = 沉默的那位终于开口了。“说说你做过的一件不光彩的事，”对方说，“以及你会不会再做一次。”
# en: A small panelled room, an interviewer who hasn't spoken leaning forward over folded hands, a student on the other side of the table very still.
scene [5eab0f] = 一间小小的镶板房间，一位始终没开口的面试官双手交握、身体前倾，桌子另一边的学生一动不动。
# en: Tell the truth
opt.left.label [d8bf00] = 说实话
# en: You tell them the truth, all of it, and what you learned, and that you wouldn't. The silent one is quiet for a long moment. "Thank you," they say, and it sounds like the end of a search.
opt.left.say.1 [8a3687] = 你说了实话，全部，还有你学到了什么，以及你不会再做。沉默的那位安静了很久。“谢谢你，”对方说，听起来像一场寻找终于结束了。
# en: You tell them the truth, and halfway through you realise you might do it again. So does the silent one. "Honest," they say. It isn't clear whether that's good.
opt.left.say.2 [694938] = 你说了实话，说到一半你意识到自己可能还会再做。沉默的那位也意识到了。“很诚实，”对方说。不清楚这是好是坏。
# en: Tell them what they want to hear
opt.right.label [2318d9] = 说他们想听的
# en: A small mistake, gracefully regretted, neatly learned from. It isn't quite true. The silent one writes something down and underlines it.
opt.right.say.1 [450ed2] = 一个小小的过失，体面地后悔，干净地吸取了教训。这不完全是真的。沉默的那位写下了什么，还划了线。
# en: The story is too neat, and the silent one has heard it before, from better liars. "I see," they say, and you hear the door closing.
opt.right.say.2 [ae64c0] = 这个故事太完美了，沉默的那位从更会撒谎的人那里听过。“我明白了，”对方说，你听见了门关上的声音。

@event y3_interview_verdict
# en: We'll Be in Touch
title [8502a1] = 我们会再联系你
# en: "We'll be in touch," says the smiling one, and stands, and so you stand too. In the corridor your legs feel like someone else's. {iv_score >= 3: You've never been so sure of anything.|{iv_score >= 2: You think it went well. You think.|{iv_score >= 1: It could have gone either way.|You know exactly how it went.}}}
text [0b6c26] = “我们会再联系你的，”爱笑的那位说着站了起来，于是你也站了起来。到了走廊里，你的腿像是别人的。{iv_score >= 3: 你从没对一件事这么有把握过。|{iv_score >= 2: 你觉得还不错。你觉得。|{iv_score >= 1: 结果可能是好是坏。|你清楚地知道结果如何。}}}
# en: A student walking out of a panelled room into a bright corridor, loosening their collar, a closed door behind them.
scene [6f60cb] = 一个学生走出镶板房间，来到明亮的走廊里，松了松领口，身后的门关着。
# en: Wait for the letter
opt.ok.label [b2e924] = 等那封信
# en: You go back to your room and lie on the bed and don't move for an hour. Somewhere, three people are deciding.
opt.ok.say.1 [bddf2b] = 你回到房间，躺在床上，一个小时一动不动。某个地方，三个人正在做决定。
# en: You go back to your room and replay every answer. The better ones get better each time; the bad ones get worse.
opt.ok.say.2 [7f2983] = 你回到房间，把每个回答都回放了一遍。好的那些每回放一次都更好，糟的那些更糟。
# en: You go back to your room and don't replay anything at all. Some things you just know.
opt.ok.say.3 [964087] = 你回到房间，什么都没有回放。有些事你就是知道。

@event y3_waitlist
# en: The Waiting List
title [b22c0d] = 候补名单
# en: A thin letter. You are "a strong candidate" and on "a short list", and they "hope to write again". It's not a no. It's not anything.
text [c3aabb] = 一封薄薄的信。你是“一位很有实力的候选人”，在“一份短名单”上，他们“希望能再次来信”。这不是拒绝。这什么也不是。
# en: A thin envelope on a dormitory desk, a single page beside it, a student reading it a second time with their chin on their fist.
scene [1828d6] = 薄薄的信封放在宿舍书桌上，旁边一页信纸，一个学生用拳头托着下巴，正读第二遍。
# en: Write back and make your case
opt.left.label [625a25] = 回信为自己争取
# en: Two pages, plain and sure: why you, why them, why now. A fortnight later, a heavier envelope.
opt.left.say.1 [7ac0fb] = 两页，朴实而笃定：为什么是你，为什么是他们，为什么是现在。两个星期后，来了一个更厚的信封。
# en: You write two pages, then four, then a fifth you shouldn't send, and do. No heavier envelope comes.
opt.left.say.2 [987fe8] = 你写了两页，然后四页，然后写了不该寄的第五页，还是寄了。更厚的信封一直没来。
# en: Let it lie and see
opt.right.label [73a78b] = 先放着，看看再说
# en: You let it lie. Two months later, when you'd almost stopped looking, the heavier envelope comes after all.
opt.right.say.1 [b8c566] = 你把它放着。两个月后，就在你快要不再留意的时候，那个更厚的信封终究还是来了。
# en: You let it lie. It stays lying. Other paths open; you try not to look back at this one.
opt.right.say.2 [080470] = 你把它放着。它就一直放着。别的路打开了；你尽量不回头看这一条。

@event y3_rejection
# en: A Polite Letter
title [d7fd3b] = 一封客气的信
# en: A short letter, very politely written. They were "impressed by your enthusiasm". They regret. They wish you every success.
text [a0b886] = 一封短信，写得非常客气。他们“对你的热情印象深刻”。他们很遗憾。他们祝你一切顺利。
# en: A crumpled letter on a windowsill, a student looking out at the lake with their arms folded.
scene [c16037] = 一封揉皱的信放在窗台上，一个学生抱着胳膊望向湖面。
# en: Ask them what went wrong
opt.left.label [7fa9d5] = 问他们哪里出了问题
# en: You write and ask. To your surprise they answer, frankly, two pages of it. It stings, and it's the most useful thing anyone's told you all year.
opt.left.say.1 [0a0ada] = 你写信去问。出乎意料，他们坦率地回答了，足足两页。这很刺痛，也是今年别人告诉你的最有用的东西。
# en: Throw it in the lake
opt.right.label [0e9dff] = 扔进湖里
# en: You fold it into a boat and launch it from the jetty. It sinks with great dignity. Some doors close; there are a great many doors.
opt.right.say.1 [dda54f] = 你把它折成一只小船，从码头放下水。它极有尊严地沉了下去。有些门关上了；门多的是。

@event y3_offer_letter
# en: The Offer
title [d66d52] = 录用通知
# en: A heavy envelope with a seal you recognise from the fair. Inside, a single page: an offer. A place. A future with a start date. {iv_score >= 3: There is a signing purse, too, which they call "a token".|} It needs a signature by the end of the month.
text [656442] = 一个厚重的信封，封蜡上的纹章你在招聘会上见过。里面只有一页纸：一份录用。一个位置。一个有开始日期的未来。{iv_score >= 3: 还附了一笔签约金，他们称之为“一点心意”。|} 月底前需要签字。
# en: An envelope with a heavy wax seal on a dormitory desk, unopened, a hand hovering over it.
scene [fc8326] = 宿舍书桌上一个盖着厚重火漆的信封，还没拆开，一只手悬在上面。
# en: Sign it today
opt.left.label [f7ce3c] = 今天就签
# en: Your signature looks strange on the page — like a grown-up's. You pin the letter above your bed and look at it every night.
opt.left.say.1 [e65e25] = 你的签名在纸上看起来很陌生——像个大人的签名。你把信钉在床头，每晚都要看一眼。
# en: Ask them to wait
opt.right.label [3eda22] = 请他们再等等
# en: You write back asking for time. They grant it, coolly. The future, it turns out, does not like waiting, but it will.
opt.right.say.1 [1ecd4d] = 你回信请求多给些时间。对方同意了，语气冷淡。原来未来不喜欢等待——但它会等的。

@event y3_first_year_mentee
# en: Your First-Year
title [891c46] = 你的一年级生
# en: Fourth-years are assigned a first-year to mentor. Yours is called Pim, is about the size of a large cat, and has already asked forty-one questions, including "are the stairs alive" and "are YOU alive".
text [0665b1] = 四年级生都会分配到一个一年级生来带。你的那个叫皮姆，个头和一只大猫差不多，已经问了四十一个问题，包括“楼梯是活的吗”和“你是活的吗”。
# en: A tiny first-year trotting beside a fourth-year across the courtyard, firing questions, clutching an enormous timetable.
scene [7ece82] = 一个小小的一年级生小跑着跟在四年级生身边穿过庭院，连珠炮似的发问，怀里紧抱着一张巨大的课表。
# en: Answer every question honestly
opt.left.label [54cf3c] = 老老实实回答每个问题
# en: Yes, the stairs are alive. Yes, you are alive. No, the lake is not "friendly". Pim takes notes. By spring, Pim is explaining things to other first-years, wrongly but with total confidence.
opt.left.say.1 [e5db2e] = 是的，楼梯是活的。是的，你是活的。不，湖并不“友好”。皮姆一一记下。到了春天，皮姆已经在给别的一年级生讲解了——讲错了，但无比自信。
# en: Teach Pim to find answers alone
opt.right.label [9c42d4] = 教皮姆自己找答案
# en: You hand Pim a library card and a map. Pim is furious for a week, then unstoppable. The librarian now knows Pim by name. And fears Pim, slightly.
opt.right.say.1 [515043] = 你递给皮姆一张借书证和一张地图。皮姆气了一个星期，然后就势不可挡了。图书管理员现在叫得出皮姆的名字。而且有一点怕皮姆。

@event y3_last_lanterns
# en: The Last Lantern Night
title [781522] = 最后一个灯笼夜
# en: Your last Lantern Night. You stand on the shore with an unlit lantern and a pen and realise you have no idea what to wish for. Three years ago it was obvious. Now it isn't.
text [a78390] = 你的最后一个灯笼夜。你站在湖岸上，手里是一盏没点的灯笼和一支笔，忽然发现自己完全不知道该许什么愿。三年前答案再明显不过。现在不是了。
# en: A lone student on the shore at night holding an unlit lantern, hundreds of others already drifting over the dark lake.
scene [2d5995] = 夜里，一名学生独自站在岸边，手捧一盏未点亮的灯笼，数百盏灯笼已经飘向漆黑的湖面。
# en: Wish for the people you'll leave behind
opt.left.label [af62f4] = 为要留下的人们许愿
# en: You write all their names. It takes the whole lantern. It rises slowly, heavily, and you watch it until it is just a star among stars.
opt.left.say.1 [a49d3f] = 你写下了他们所有人的名字，写满了整盏灯笼。它缓缓地、沉甸甸地升起，你一直望着它，直到它变成群星中的一颗。
# en: Leave it blank
opt.right.label [54fbdb] = 留白
# en: You let it go empty. Strangely, it rises higher than all the others. Maybe the lake likes not knowing either.
opt.right.say.1 [154e37] = 你放走了一盏空灯笼。奇怪的是，它比其他所有灯笼都升得更高。也许湖也喜欢不知道答案。

@event y3_thesis
# en: The Last Chapter
title [87e9c9] = 最后一章
# en: Your thesis needs one more chapter. You could write something safe and solid, or chase the question your sources keep circling and nobody has answered in three hundred years: why the academy was built above a lake.
text [5724af] = 你的论文还差最后一章。你可以写点稳妥扎实的东西，也可以去追那个你的资料总在打转、三百年来无人解答的问题：学院为什么要建在湖上？
# en: A desk buried in drafts, a wall of pinned notes connected by string, a single candle and a single exhausted student.
scene [df58af] = 一张被草稿淹没的书桌，一面钉满笔记、用细绳相连的墙，一支蜡烛，一个筋疲力尽的学生。
# en: Safe and solid
opt.left.label [f81e8e] = 稳妥扎实
# en: Forty pages on the thermodynamics of hovering charms. Impeccable. Unremarkable. Your examiners will sleep well.
opt.left.say.1 [fe97ef] = 四十页论悬浮咒的热力学。无可挑剔，平平无奇。你的考官们会睡得很香。
# en: The question nobody answered
opt.right.label [e94f06] = 那个无人解答的问题
# en: The chapter is so good that your supervisor shows it round the staff room, and the headmistress asks for the only copy — and then, very politely, does not give it back.
opt.right.say.1 [e0a83d] = 这一章好到导师拿着它在教员休息室里到处给人看，院长还亲自索要了唯一的一份——然后，非常客气地，没有还回来。
# en: You chase the question until it runs out of archive. The chapter ends mid-sentence, like the founders' ledger. The examiners are not amused.
opt.right.say.2 [044bc6] = 你追着这个问题一直追到档案的尽头。这一章在一句话中间戛然而止，就像创始者的账簿。考官们一点也不觉得有趣。

@event y3_portrait
# en: Sitting for the Portrait
title [a99086] = 坐着画像
# en: Every graduate's portrait hangs in the long gallery — and every portrait, eventually, starts talking. You have one sitting to decide who will be gossiping on that wall for the next three hundred years.
text [d9377f] = 每位毕业生的画像都会挂在长廊里——而每幅画像迟早都会开口说话。你只有一次坐下来的机会，来决定接下来三百年在那面墙上说闲话的会是什么样的人。
# en: An old painter at an easel in a sunlit studio, a student posing stiffly in robes, half-finished portraits of past graduates watching from the walls.
scene [2a1426] = 阳光充足的画室里，一位老画家站在画架前，一名身着长袍的学生僵硬地摆着姿势，往届毕业生未完成的画像从墙上注视着他们。
# en: Pose solemn and dignified
opt.left.label [f39072] = 庄重得体地摆姿势
# en: The painter captures you looking wise and distant. Your portrait will be dignified. It will also be dreadfully bored.
opt.left.say.1 [af471d] = 画家画出了你睿智而疏远的神情。你的画像会很体面。它也会无聊得要命。
# en: Pose as yourself, mid-laugh
opt.right.label [e9bd51] = 做你自己，笑到一半
# en: Your portrait is laughing. Three days after it's hung, it starts telling the other portraits jokes. The gallery has never been louder.
opt.right.say.1 [c325e4] = 你的画像在笑。挂上去三天后，它开始给其他画像讲笑话。长廊从来没有这么吵过。

@event y3_letter_to_self
# en: A Letter to Your First-Year Self
title [64655e] = 写给一年级的自己
# en: The Divination department runs a tradition: write a letter to your first-year self. They swear it will be delivered. Nobody knows how. Some fourth-years swear they received theirs.
text [eb06b6] = 占卜系有个传统：给一年级的自己写一封信。他们发誓信一定会送到，没人知道是怎么送的。有些四年级生发誓自己收到过。
# en: A fourth-year writing by candlelight, a box of keepsakes open beside them: a pressed flower, a ticket stub, a borrowed wand returned.
scene [61521a] = 一个四年级生在烛光下写信，身旁打开着一个纪念品盒子：一朵压花、一张票根、一根借来又还掉的魔杖。
# en: Tell them it'll be all right
opt.left.label [c88d16] = 告诉自己一切都会好的
# en: You write: "It's going to be all right. Not easy. All right." The next morning the letter is gone, and you remember, very faintly, reading it once on a sky-barge.
opt.left.say.1 [1f6e42] = 你写道：“会好起来的。不会容易，但会好起来。”第二天早上信不见了，而你隐约记起，自己曾在一艘天空驳船上读过它。
# en: You try to write something comforting, and it keeps coming out as a list of warnings. You seal it anyway. The next morning it is gone.
opt.left.say.2 [8efc83] = 你想写些安慰的话，可写出来总像一张警告清单。你还是把信封好了。第二天早上，它不见了。
# en: Warn them about everything
opt.right.label [065681] = 把所有事都警告一遍
# en: You write eleven pages of warnings. The letter is returned unopened with a note in Divination ink: "Some things must be learned the hard way."
opt.right.say.1 [4ed2e4] = 你写了十一页的警告。信原封未动地退了回来，附着一张用占卜墨水写的字条：“有些事必须吃过苦头才学得会。”

@event y3_maud_seeds
# en: Seeds for Later
title [6b0198] = 留给以后的种子
# en: Maud presses a paper packet into your hands. "Seeds," she says. "From the secret garden. Plant them wherever you end up. They'll grow anywhere someone is a bit kind to them." She sniffs. "Like you did."
text [59075b] = 莫德把一个纸包塞进你手里。“种子，”她说，“秘密花园里的。不管你最后去了哪儿，都种下去。只要有人对它们好一点，它们在哪儿都能长。”她吸了吸鼻子。“就像你一样。”
# en: An old woman pressing a small paper packet of seeds into a student's hands at the garden gate, bees drifting in the evening light.
scene [f66df9] = 花园门口，一位老妇人把一小包种子按进学生手里，暮色中蜜蜂缓缓飞舞。
# en: Hug her
opt.left.label [042130] = 拥抱她
# en: She protests for exactly one second and then hugs back, fierce and small and smelling of rosemary. "Go on," she says. "Before I get soppy."
opt.left.say.1 [51b153] = 她抗议了整整一秒钟，然后用力回抱你，又小又结实，带着迷迭香的味道。“去吧，”她说，“趁我还没变得肉麻。”
# en: Promise to come back and visit
opt.right.label [17c08e] = 答应回来看她
# en: "Every summer," you promise. "We'll see," she says, but she writes it on her calendar, in ink, which for Maud is a blood oath.
opt.right.say.1 [96e47e] = “每年夏天都来，”你保证。“走着瞧，”她说，却把这件事写在了日历上——用墨水写的，对莫德来说这等于血誓。

@event y3_last_duel
# en: One Last Duel
title [15df69] = 最后一场决斗
# en: Dawn, the empty dueling ring, no crowd. Lyra is waiting. "No referee," she says. "No points. Just one last duel, for us. So we know."
text [5b0db9] = 黎明，空荡荡的决斗场，没有观众。莱拉在等你。“没有裁判，”她说，“不计分。就最后一场决斗，为了我们自己。这样我们就知道了。”
# en: Two duelists bowing in an empty dueling ring at dawn, no crowd, no referee, just the mist and the lake beyond.
scene [b6c6d5] = 黎明时分，两名决斗者在空无一人的决斗场里互相鞠躬，没有观众，没有裁判，只有薄雾和远处的湖。
# en: Duel her with everything
opt.left.label [9ed8a1] = 全力以赴和她决斗
# en: It lasts eleven minutes. Nobody wins. You both end up flat on your backs, laughing at the sky. "Now we know," she says.
opt.left.say.1 [e4826f] = 打了十一分钟。没有人赢。最后你们俩都仰面躺在地上，对着天空大笑。“现在我们知道了，”她说。
# en: She wins, cleanly. Then she helps you up and doesn't let go of your hand for a moment longer than necessary. "Now we know."
opt.left.say.2 [cc0906] = 她干净利落地赢了。然后她把你拉起来，握着你的手比必要的多停了一会儿。“现在我们知道了。”
# en: Lower your wand and just talk
opt.right.label [075cd4] = 放下魔杖，只是聊聊
# en: You talk until the mist burns off. About fire, and mothers, and what comes after. You both miss the morning lecture. It turns out you didn't need to duel to know.
opt.right.say.1 [e438e7] = 你们一直聊到薄雾散尽。聊火焰，聊母亲，聊以后的事。你们俩都错过了早课。原来不需要决斗也能知道。

@event y3_time_capsule
# en: The Time Capsule
title [f63962] = 时间胶囊
# en: Your friends have a battered tin box, a shovel and a plan: bury a time capsule under the old oak, to be opened in twenty years. Everyone puts something in. What will you give?
text [950958] = 你的朋友们带来了一个破旧的铁皮盒、一把铲子和一个计划：在老橡树下埋一个时间胶囊，二十年后再打开。每个人都要放点东西进去。你放什么？
# en: A group of students kneeling around a hole under an old oak, lowering in a battered tin box sealed with wax.
scene [cd24b8] = 一群学生跪在老橡树下的坑边，把一个用蜡封好的破铁皮盒放进去。
# en: Something precious
opt.left.label [3a8593] = 放一件珍贵的东西
# en: You put in the first thing you ever enchanted. It's ugly and crooked and it still hums. Someone cries, and blames the dirt.
opt.left.say.1 [1fe988] = 你放进了你施过魔法的第一件东西。它又丑又歪，至今还在嗡嗡作响。有人哭了，然后怪是土进了眼睛。
# en: Something ridiculous
opt.right.label [957c3e] = 放一件荒唐的东西
# en: You put in a single sock, labelled "EVIDENCE". In twenty years, nobody will remember why. That's the point.
opt.right.say.1 [fa92c3] = 你放进了一只袜子，上面贴着标签：“证物”。二十年后，没人会记得为什么。这正是意义所在。

@event y3_speech
# en: The Graduation Speech
title [ffc856] = 毕业致辞
# en: The headmistress catches you in the great hall, where chairs are already being set out. "Each year one graduate speaks for their class," she says. "This year, the faculty would like it to be you."
text [eebc6f] = 院长在大礼堂里叫住了你，那里已经开始摆椅子了。“每年都由一位毕业生代表全班致辞，”她说，“今年，教职员们希望是你。”
# en: A headmistress handing a scroll to a student in an empty great hall, rows of chairs set out for a ceremony that hasn't happened yet.
scene [9ef184] = 空荡荡的大礼堂里，一位院长把一卷纸递给一名学生，一排排椅子已为尚未举行的典礼摆好。
# en: Accept and write something honest
opt.left.label [d1eed2] = 接受，写些真心话
# en: You write about fear, and friends, and the lake, and the things you didn't know you'd miss. When you practise it alone, your voice cracks in the same place every time. You leave it in.
opt.left.say.1 [35d90b] = 你写恐惧，写朋友，写湖，写那些你从不知道自己会怀念的东西。独自练习时，你的声音每次都在同一个地方哽住。你把它留在了稿子里。
# en: Decline — someone else deserves it
opt.right.label [121bee] = 婉拒——值得的另有其人
# en: "Interesting," says the headmistress, which from her is a medal. The speech goes to a nervous first-generation student who absolutely brings the house down.
opt.right.say.1 [9ddc3d] = “有意思，”院长说——从她嘴里说出来，这就是一枚勋章。致辞的机会给了一位紧张的、家里第一代上学的学生，那位学生把全场都点燃了。
